    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "Roval",
      "COCKTAILS\nLama ho' ohuihui'ia\nMAI TAI\nHere's a fabulous South Seas potion that embodies the rich romance\nand haunting beauty of Hawaii. Using the original recipe, we've combined the\nsunny glow of rum with the fresh flavors of several tropical fruits.\nSip! And dream of sunset on the reef.\nMENEHUNE JUICE\nIf you're going to catch even a fleeting glimpse of those elusive little Menchunes,\nyou have to be in the right place at the right time-and in the right light-hearted mood.\nThat's why we invented Menehune Juice. Its blend of tropic flavors conjures up a\nvision of a rain forest with sunlight filtering through the leaves.\nand a touch of light, flavorful rum completes the spell. Drink and be ready!\nUNITED'S VERY DRY BEEFEATER MARTINI\nUNITED'S VERY DRY SMIRNOFF VODKA MARTINI\nMANHATTAN BLOODY MARY SCREWDRIVER DRY SACK SHERRY\nCHRISTIAN BROTHERS BRANDY DOMESTIC BEER\nSPIRITS Wai Kulu\nBACARDI RUM BEEFEATER GIN DEWAR'S WHITE LABEL SCOTCH\nCHIVAS REGAL JACK DANIEL'S TENNESSEE WHISKEY OLD GRAND-DAD\nCANADIAN CLUB SMIRNOFF VODKA\nWINES\nWaina\nALMADÉN BRUT CHAMPAGNE\nALMADÉN CABERNET SAUVIGNON\nPAUL MASSON PINOT CHARDONNAY\nLIQUEURS War oma\nAMARETTO DI SARONNO BAILEYS IRISH CREAM\nBENEDICTINE AND BRANDY\nCAMUS COGNAC DRAMBUIE\nGRAND MARNIER KAHLUA\nBEVERAGES Meainu\nMaxwell House Coffee\nSanka®\nTEA\nMILK\nGUAVA JUICE\nSOFT BEVERAGES\nCoca-Cola\nMinors Cannot Be Served Alcohol.\nAPPETIZERS Pupu\nSelection of popular Hawaiian style pupus for your enjoyment\nwith your favorite cocktail.\nBARBECUED RIBS\nCHICKEN PARADISE\nKALUA PORK CREPE\nSALAD OFFERING Lau'alia\nKAMAAINA SALAD, JAVANESE DRESSING\nSliced celery, hearts of palm, king crab and fresh mushrooms,\ntossed and served on a slice of beef steak tomato with butter lettuce.\nROYAL HAWAIIAN ENTREE SELECTIONS\nROAST STRIP SIRLOIN OF BEEF, AU JUS\nWe start with USDA choice sirloin of beef, rub it with herbs and spices, then roast it in its\nnatural juices. This favorite will be carved at your seat... for the perfect accompaniment\ntry our mild horseradish sauce.\nSAVOYARD POTATOES, CAULIFLOWER FLORETTES AND TOMATO CLAMART\nROAST LONG ISLAND DUCKLING, A LORANGE\nA partially boned breast and thigh are well roasted and\ntopped with orange sauce.\nBROWN AND WILD RICE, WHOLE GREEN BEANS\nOSSO BUCO\nA sliced veal shank, bone-in, braised with finely diced vegetables.\nserved with a brown sauce. Accompanied with rice\nand served with broccoli florettes.\nOUR LIGHTER AIR FARE\nToday's selection is an array of fresh fruits in season.\ntastefully arranged and served with cottage cheese.\nA SELECTION OF WARMED DINNER ROLLS WILL BE PRESENTED.\nDESSERT Mea'ai momona\nWARM APPLE STRUDEL SERVED WITH VANILLA ICE CREAM\nFRESH HAWAIIAN PINEAPPLE\nFreshly cut Hawaiian pineapple is a lighter alternative.\nFRESH FRUIT BASKET\nIt has been our pleasure to prepare this repast for your enjoyment.\nCarmine P. Maffei, Certified Executive Chef, United Airlines Flight Kitchen at San Francisco International Airport\nMember, American Culinary Federation: Chefs Association of the Pacific Coast: Chaine Des Rotisseus\n1/D31-1"
    ],
